      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Founded in March 1871, the Upton Town Library began in a converted church downtown and moved to a new building in 2023.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Upton%2C_Massachusetts",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Polly Dean Bradish House, built in 1844, served as one of only two known Underground Railroad stations in Upton.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.achp.gov/preserve-america/community/upton-massachusetts",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Upton Historical Society preserves artifacts, photographs, and recordings that chronicle the town’s history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
